# XMPL100 Driver

C++20 driver for the XMPL100, a fictional example SPI temperature sensor: chip ID, one-shot and continuous reads, CRC.

[![CI](https://github.com/kokeb-labs/driver-template/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg?branch=main)](https://github.com/kokeb-labs/driver-template/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue)](LICENSE)
[![C++20](https://img.shields.io/badge/C%2B%2B-20-informational)](docs/installation.md#requirements)

**Documentation: <https://kokeb-labs.github.io/driver-template/>**

The XMPL100 is an analog temperature sensor: its output voltage rises 10 mV for every degree, from 500 mV at 0 °C.
This driver powers it up, checks that a sensor is really on the ADC channel, averages several conversions and turns
the voltage into degrees with the datasheet's transfer function or your calibration. It runs on any MCU: you give it
a small class that reads one ADC channel in millivolts, and it does the rest.

