## At a glance

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **Chip** | XMPL100 analog temperature sensor |
| **Measures** | Temperature, -40 °C to +125 °C, as 500 mV at 0 °C plus 10 mV/°C (typical) |
| **Bus** | None: one analog output to an MCU ADC channel |
| **Also drives** | SHDN_N, when your port has `GpioSet()` |
| **Driver** | Header-only C++20; no heap, exceptions, RTTI or virtual calls; every call returns `Result<T>` |
| **Runs on** | Any MCU with an ADC and a C++20 compiler; the host example runs on any PC ([Platforms](docs/platforms.md)) |
| **Status** | 0.1.0, not yet verified on hardware: host-tested against a model of the output |

